``
Wait — careful with gh-823: "hoist every require to the top of the module". Top-level in the reporter = module init → file-relative resolution ✓. But the test loader `loadReporter` mocks only './configLoader.js' — with makeRequire, unmapped ids THROW. I must update `loadReporter` in the test file to map the new modules (load the real ones via loadModule). That's acceptable — but wait, there are ~30 calls to loadReporter in the test file; updating the single helper covers all. 

Hmm, but do I really want the reporter to require factory/token_usage.js? What do I take from it: shellQuote, bootstrapBranchCommand, contentsShaCommand, contentsBodyCommand, contentsPutCommand, ROW_KEEP, DEFAULT_WINDOW_DAYS, utcStampZ?, cutoffIso?. utcStampZ/cutoffIso are trivial; reusing keeps ONE transport vocabulary (the ticket: "same publish shape as fa's gh-781 producer"). Yes, require it.

And teammateEventDedup for issueOfRunName/legOfRunName — the ONE title-parsing vocabulary. Yes.

BUT — pack closure consideration: dmtools compile discovers the pack closure file-relative from the entry config jsPath `agents/js/aiTeammateTokenUsageReporter.js`. Top-level requires resolve file-relative at init → `agents/js/common/teammateEventDedup.js` + `agents/js/factory/token_usage.js` — both inside the pack ✓.

